  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This CPO aims to address critical challenges in workers&apos; and trade union rights in Kyrgyzstan, fostering alignment with international labour standards. Through targeted initiatives, the independence and functionality of trade unions will be enhanced, adherence to ILO conventions will be promoted, and labour protections across sectors will be strengthened.
Key outcomes include the strengthening of the Federation of Trade Unions of Kyrgyzstan (FTUKG), with joint efforts focused on reforms to improve compliance with international labour standards (ILS) and enhance the exercise of freedom of association (FOA) and collective bargaining (CB). Through policy advice and technical assistance, the FTUKG will be supported to democratize and modernize its internal regulations and structure, expand representation to include workers from emerging sectors, women, and youth, and strengthen protections and innovative services for informal and non-unionized workers. A priority area is the implementation of ILO Convention 190 on violence and harassment in the workplace, ratified by Kyrgyzstan and set to take effect in June 2025. Additionally, the FTUKG and sectoral unions including in textiles and mining will be supported in advancing Freedom of Association, effective collective bargaining, green energy transition, occupational safety and health (OSH), and gender equality.</narrative>
  </description>
